- **So, the rule:** a value that must LOOK real to your own scanner (the token of S04, any high-entropy value) is BUILT AT RUN TIME by the test from parts (encode a header object, a payload object and random bytes, join with dots; random letters from the framework's generator); it is never a literal in a tracked file. A value that need not look real is an OBVIOUSLY FAKE literal that holds the word `SYNTHETIC` or `synthetic`. No real-looking e-mail address (use the reserved domain `example.invalid`), no real person's name, no host name of Datasec, HP or Microsoft.
